  "rule_id": "ya_idafa_iskan_exception",
  "version": "1",
  "name_ar": "ياءات الإضافة الساكنة استثناء",
  "definition": "First-person ya read with sukun although it precedes a hamza or hamzat al-wasl: eight words before a fatha hamza (فاذكروني، أرني، تفتني، ترحمني، فاتبعني، أوزعني ×2، ذروني، ادعوني), eight before a kasra hamza (أنظرني، يدعونني، إخوتي، فأنظرني ×2، يصدقني، تدعونني ×2، ذريتي، أخرتني), two before a damma hamza (بعهدي، آتوني), and three before hamzat al-wasl with no article (إني، أخي، ليتني).",
  "riwaya": "qaloun",
  "tariq": "unspecified",
  "family": "ya_idafa",
  "detectability": "C",
  "limitations": [
    "Paraphrase of the cited pages by an automated drafter; not scholarly reviewed.",
    "Only Book A is cited; the printed page is where the section begins and needs proofreading.",
    "A closed list in the Kufian numbering used by the book.",
    "The book disagrees with itself on four places. Each word was looked up in the corpus: (1) تدعونني: p.46 item 13 gives Ghafir 43 only, p.49 item 6 gives 41 and 43; the word is in both, both are kept. (2) أنظرني: p.46 item 6 gives al-A'raf 40, p.49 item 1 gives 14; the word is in 7:14 only, 7:14 is kept. (3) فأنظرني: p.46 item 6 gives Sad 79, p.49 item 4 gives Sad 147, which does not exist; the word is in 38:79, kept. (4) أوزعني: p.49 item 6 gives al-Ahqaf 14; the word is in 46:15, with ذريتي (p.46 item 15), and not in 46:14, so 46:15 is kept. The count of 21 on p.46 lists only 20 places because of (1)."
  ],
